cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "T4: Can LLMs Generate Retry-Safe Payment Services? — A Fault-Injection Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  T4 is a deterministic fault-injection benchmark for evaluating whether
  generated payment services are retry-safe under crashes, dropped provider
  acknowledgements, unknown (timeout) outcomes, and concurrent retries. It ships
  a single-process deterministic-simulation harness, seven Tier-1 task families
  (each with one correct reference and five seeded-bug mutants), a shared oracle
  checking six financial-safety invariants, and public plus hidden fault
  schedules. This artifact accompanies a double-blind IEEE submission.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
version: "0.1.0-pilot"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - fault injection
  - deterministic simulation
  - idempotency
  - retry safety
  - payment systems
  - large language models
  - code generation
